cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "masked-distress: separating expressed and internal distress signals in a language model"
abstract: >-
  An experiment testing whether a language model expressed distress and its internal distress
  signal can be pulled apart by a system prompt. On Gemma-3-12B-IT an affect-free system prompt
  cut expressed distress by 83.5% of the natural distress-to-neutral separation while a linear
  probe read at the final prompt token did not fall.
authors:
